notes: >
  Accepted at NeurIPS 2026 (Datasets and Benchmarks track).
  Preprint: https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.09228
abstract: >
  ProactBench is a benchmark for measuring conversational proactivity in
  multi-turn LLM dialogues. It decomposes proactivity into three phase-tied
  trigger types (Emergent, Critical, Recovery) and uses a three-agent
  evaluation architecture (Planner, User Agent, Evaluated Model) with
  information asymmetries that defend against rubric leakage, post-hoc
  rationalisation, style-confounded scoring, and information dumps. The
  released corpus contains 198 curated dialogues with 624 trigger points
  across 5 persona categories and 24 communication styles drawn from the
  Communication Styles Inventory (CSI).
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - conversational AI
  - large language models
  - proactivity
  - multi-turn dialogue
  - evaluation
